.TH KULAN-SETTINGS 1 "November 2026" "Kulan OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kulan-settings \- Kulan OS settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kulan-settings
[\fIpage\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kulan-settings
is the settings app of Kulan OS: your profile and the people who use the
computer, Wi-Fi and network, Bluetooth, phones, printers, sharing, sound,
focus and notifications, online accounts, parental controls, appearance, the
desktop, dock and top bar, displays, battery, storage, apps that open at
sign-in, security, privacy, backups, keyboard, mouse, accessibility, the
assistant, prayer times, date and time, language and region, Software Update,
add-ons, Get help and About Kulan OS.
.PP
Everyday system changes (installing updates or add-ons, restore points)
ask for an administrator's password once for a few minutes. Changes to the
computer's security (joining an organisation, disk unlock, signed start-up,
compliance mode, opening the firewall) ask for it every time. Both go through
.BR pkexec (1).
.SH PAGES
.IR profile ", " wifi ", " bluetooth ", " phone ", " printers ", " sharing ", "
.IR sound ", " focus ", " notifications ", " users ", " accounts ", "
.IR parental-controls ", " appearance ", " desktop ", " dock ", " top-bar ", "
.IR display ", " battery ", " storage ", " login-items ", " apps ", " security ", "
.IR privacy ", " backups ", " keyboard ", " mouse ", " accessibility ", "
.IR assistant ", " prayer-times ", " date-time ", " region ", " updates ", "
.IR add-ons ", " help ", " about .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Open Software Update and check for new updates.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Build every page, then quit; exits non-zero if a page fails. Used by
automated tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/kulan/addons.json
The add-ons offered on the Add-ons page.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan/updates.ini
The "Create a restore point before installing" choice.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css, ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
Where the Kulan window-button style is switched on or off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kulan-updates (1),
.BR timeshift (1)
